2. Where do they get the odds? (The Source)
The absolute "top of the food chain" for odds data are the B2B Odds Feed Providers. These companies employ thousands of data scouts and use complex AI models to generate the prices. The most prominent ones are:

Sportradar (Betradar): The global leader. They provide the "Managed Trading Services" (MTS) that power the majority of the world's sportsbooks.

Genius Sports: Major rivals to Sportradar, especially strong in US sports and official league data.

Abios & PandaScore: These are the "specialists" for Esports. If you see deep markets for CS2 or Valorant, the odds are likely coming from one of these two.

Betfair Exchange: Many bookmakers also scrape the Betfair Exchange API to see where the "sharp" money is moving and adjust their own prices accordingly.
 

API
PandaScore: Offers a dedicated Esports API with a free tier for developers. 


